  "doc.title": "What Is Actually Travelling When a Signal Crosses Empty Space · A Hands-on Essay",
  "doc.desc": "Voyager 1 is one light-day away with nothing in between, and its signal still arrives. This essay starts from electric and magnetic fields: how Maxwell's four laws make a wave that carries itself, how the speed of light falls out of two bench-top constants, how waves are radiated, what they carry, and what matter and the atmosphere do to them; then modulation, link budgets, optical fibre, the diffraction limit and phased arrays, and the frontier as of 2026. Fourteen hands-on models, each the real equation at small scale.",
